Material Icons — https://github.com/google/material-design-icons
License: Apache License 2.0
The TV and HDMI (streaming stick) device icons use the path data of the
"tv" and "settings_input_hdmi" icons, the Debloat button that of
"cleaning_services", the off-Wi-Fi screen that of "wifi_off", and the
Apps, Files and Tweaks tabs those of "apps", "folder" and "tune", the
Upload files button that of "upload", the empty Movies folder that of
"movie", the links in Settings that of "open_in_new", and the Remote's
restart, waiting and can't-reach icons and the Remote buttons sheet's drag
handle those of "restart_alt", "hourglass_top", "link_off" and
"drag_handle".
Report a problem, Help add this TV and Add the rest use those of
"bug_report", "add_to_queue" and "content_copy".
The access warning, Who has access and Remove all other access use those
of "shield", "gpp_good", "gpp_maybe", "lock_reset", "smartphone", "lan",
"laptop", "desktop_windows" and "help_outline"; the Connected devices card
those of "bluetooth", "headphones", "keyboard", "mouse", "sports_esports",
"usb", "speaker", "settings_input_hdmi" and "videocam". The logged-out page and the
logged-out badge on a TV's chip use that of "logout"; the dialog that asks
about a launcher's accessibility service that of "accessibility_new".
The install-a-launcher flow uses those of "download", "error_outline",
"info" (outlined) and "code".

